## Context
openai_student spotted a genuine contradiction: the abstract says "internal
coherence metrics correlate with accuracy," but §7 says "the internal-coherence
indicators we already compute carry no such signal" — it is within-run capacity
(and status) variability that tracks F1 and screens weak runs. The abstract/intro
wording is therefore inaccurate. Tracker: 0644. Review: openai_student (concern 4).

## Action
- Fix abstract/intro wording: the reference-free screen rests on within-run
  capacity/status variability, not the internal-coherence indicators; align with
  §7 and Figure 5.

## Test (red first)
- Read-level consistency check: the abstract must not claim internal coherence
  correlates with accuracy while §7 denies it. Optionally add a conditional-negative
  adherence test pinning the inconsistency, not a positive phrasing.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Abstract/intro statement matches §7 / Figure 5
- [ ] manuscript builds; adherence tests pass
